{
	"_note": "Nishiki Hill above Kaminoda, the valley's place to see the cherry blossom in spring and the maples in fall (the hamlet north of the village), up its lane at x 22-23 (added 2026-11-01 when the world was widened): a path switching back and forth up the slope between cherries and maples (the `sakura` and `maple` props, solid, 1 x 1; laid once by a seeded script on 2026-11-17 in place of the old bamboo groves and kept here as data; a small bamboo stand is left at the foot, x 1-7, rows 21-27; the slope just below the lookout, x 12-28, rows 3-10, is left open so the view is clear); later that day thickened (trees may stand diagonally next to each other, never side by side, and a cell off the paths) and ginkgos added: a gold avenue along the upper path's east run and a pair by the lookout, x 12 and 26, row 2. The cliff along the top is gone (the user, 2026-11-17: the trees are enough to close the hill in): rows 0-1 are grass under a band of trees in a checker two rows deep (small ones behind the lookout, x 13-26, so the mountains show over them); no pines (their seven cells hold cherries, maples and ginkgos, and the wood past the edges is all broadleaf: data/vista.json apron_trees); every tree has a `scale` (0.5-1.2: small, middling, big and a few grand ones mixed) to a lookout of raked gravel at the top, with a little mountain shrine (hokora) and two stone lanterns. Examine the shrine and the view (data/events/triggers_hill.json). Format: README.md, Maps.",
